```

This implementation uses two stacks: one to store all the elements (`stack`) and another to keep track of the minimum elements (`min_stack`). The `push` method adds an element to both stacks if necessary, ensuring that the top of the `min_stack` always contains the minimum value in the `stack`. The `pop` method removes the top element from both stacks if it is the current minimum. The `top` method simply returns the top element of the `stack`, and the `get_min` method returns the top element of the `min_stack`, which is the current minimum value in the stack. This approach ensures that all operations are performed in constant time, O(1).
